{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_023 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieved 0.535 acc / 0.519 F1, a clear ~5-point improvement over the rna_only baseline (config_005: 0.485/0.464), confirming that the image modality with ViT-L and concat fusion is beneficial. The largest untested design axis is whether moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with aggregation can further improve performance. Question: Does multiprofile + avgpool aggregation, while holding RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and fusion (concat) constant, improve over the singleprofile baseline? Why this experiment: config_003 is the minimal, clean extension of config_023 along the profile/aggregation axis, changing only profile_setting (single→multi) and adding avgpool aggregation. This isolates the multiprofile effect before introducing the more complex transformer aggregation or a different fusion strategy. If multiprofile+avgpool helps, we can then test transformer aggregation (config_017) or weighted fusion; if it does not, we save budget by avoiding more complex aggregation variants. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget."
}

